	(text "1. RTL8156BG-CG  USB 3.2 Gen1 (5G) <-> 2.5GBASE-T MAC/PHY, QFN-56 6x6 0.35 mm, EP = GND (via array)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 15.24 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.0 2.0)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "ce20a33f-d297-51a8-a46c-c1f141cb9714")
	)
	(text "Pin 9 (AVDD33 next to the XTAL) is fed through a ferrite bead (PLL supply, Realtek ref 'AVDD33_PLL')."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 167.64 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "01be2690-3c52-5591-951b-79a224df86ac")
	)
	(text "DVDD09_UPS (54) is an INTERNAL LDO output: 1 uF only, never tie to the 0.95 V rail."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 170.18 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "eb42b5be-886e-563a-836b-19c9614ed546")
	)
	(text "NC: 3/4/6 (BGS-only regulator pins), CKOUT, LED3, GPIO3, EEDO/SPISO, TWSI_SDA/SPICSB (no EEPROM/flash on the PHY)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 172.72 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "fc2d92bc-f0df-5f1e-9b83-8a04f28595e2")
	)
	(text "2. POWER  ETH_3V3 = +3V3 via TPS22918 (ON = ETH_RESET_N)   ETH_0V95 = TPS62A02A (EN = POW_EXT_SWR)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 203.2 22.86 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.0 2.0)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "290b35ff-2351-5133-b8d7-040a1cce9e91")
	)
	(text "RTL8156BG 0.95 V: 0.92-0.98 V (+-3 %), 364 mA typ / 650 mA max; rise 0.5-2.2 ms; off->on >= 50 ms (DS table 25/27)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 203.2 81.28 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "c768a878-027f-5244-ba81-2a9c39934d58")
	)
	(text "VOUT = 0.6 V x (1 + 59k/100k) = 0.954 V; VFB +-1.5 % + 1 % resistors -> 0.932-0.977 V worst case (inside window)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 203.2 83.82 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "e458b856-9525-5808-b7b5-21e021d691bb")
	)
	(text "TPS62A02A = forced-PWM variant (Realtek: switcher feeding the PHY must run PWM >= 1 MHz); 1 ms soft start meets t3."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 203.2 86.36 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "f41c2f33-3664-504d-bdcc-af4dc881b17f")
	)
	(text "The buck runs from ETH_3V3, so ETH_RESET_N low also kills 0.95 V; EN = POW_EXT_SWR (PHY output, 100k PD)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 203.2 88.9 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "7fc2b187-2960-518a-80c5-a6bf5c6027e5")
	)
	(text "ETH_RESET_N (TCA9534 P5 on mcu, 10k PU there): high/hi-Z = PHY powered -> Ethernet works with a dead/blank RP2350."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 203.2 91.44 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "ae956790-1eb7-57ea-bc72-26ccbfbd25bd")
	)
	(text "  Firmware: hold low >= 100 ms (t4 >= 50 ms + QOD discharge). Also usable to turn 2.5GbE off for thermal derating."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 203.2 93.98 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "af0a45d5-7a65-5f11-93dc-d9f19889f555")
	)
	(text "Loss: 0.95 V x 0.65 A / ~85 % -> ~0.11 W in the buck; PHY total ~0.6-0.65 W typ (sensors sheet: TMP1075 'RJ45/RTL8156')."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 203.2 96.52 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "5d499055-de88-5c9d-af2e-8f50a3449068")
	)
	(text "3. DECOUPLING  every cap at its pin (0402, short via to the GND EP/plane); bulk per Realtek reference"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 190.5 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.0 2.0)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "afc750d1-b48a-509f-8f1e-0033aa95b5c1")
	)
	(text "4. CLOCK / RSET / STRAPS (pull values from Realtek RTL8125B ref + verified open RTL8156B design)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 203.2 106.68 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.0 2.0)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "9d0af8cd-2557-5221-984a-9b092097c22b")
	)
	(text "Straps/pulls go to ETH_3V3 (never +3V3) so nothing back-powers the PHY while ETH_RESET_N holds it off."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 203.2 162.56 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "a97ffe19-6444-5f6e-b41a-c79855219c83")
	)
	(text "Crystal: same YXC 25 MHz/12 pF part as the hub (shared reel). Keep XI/XO short, GND guard, no traces under it."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 203.2 165.1 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "924814fd-7ab4-52e3-8ec4-22568808c405")
	)
	(text "5. USB  PHY TX -> 100 nF -> hub RX (hub TX caps on usb_hub)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 406.4 22.86 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.0 2.0)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "d98a22f2-d293-573f-a073-89e90c06194a")
	)
	(text "Hub port 4 (ETH_*): longest SS run on the board (around the hub's PF side). 90 Ohm diff, caps near the PHY,"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 406.4 50.8 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "28db223a-6f46-5aa9-a241-438b25d142d6")
	)
	(text "symmetric, L2 void under the 0402 pads. USB2 ETH_DP/DN: 90 Ohm, no series parts. The PHY is Gen1 (5 Gbps):"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 406.4 53.34 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "5b9b746a-0d0b-58be-bfe7-dd6570d5ca15")
	)
	(text "Gen1 C_AC_COUPLING = 75-200 nF -> 100 nF (same as the GL3224 TX); 220 nF is only valid for Gen2 transmitters."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 406.4 55.88 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
